---
import { DECISION, DECISION_META, REFERENCED_ISSUE as ISSUE } from '@lib/features/project-knowledge-base';
---

<section class="border-t border-line" aria-labelledby="kb-before-title">
  <div class="wrap py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-[640px]">
      <h2 id="kb-before-title" class="h2">
        The next person sees the runbook beside the issue.
      </h2>
      <p class="prose mt-5">
        Without a reference, <code>ACME-12</code> says what broke and nothing about why it matters. Once an article
        names it, the issue lists that article, so whoever opens it next finds the reasoning without asking around.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 md:mt-14 grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 lg:gap-8">
      <figure>
        <figcaption class="text-sm text-fg-2">
          <strong class="font-medium text-fg">Before.</strong> No article names the issue.
        </figcaption>
        <div class="panel mt-3 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="pane-bar">
            <span class="mono text-xs">ACME</span>
            <span class="sep">/</span>
            <span>Issues</span>
            <span class="sep">/</span>
            <span class="mono text-xs text-fg">{ISSUE.key}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="wf-body">
            <h3 class="wf-title mt-0">{ISSUE.title}</h3>
            <dl class="fields">
              <dt>Assignee</dt>
              <dd>
                <span class="av" aria-hidden="true">
                  {ISSUE.assignee.initials}
                </span>
                {ISSUE.assignee.name}
              </dd>
              <dt>Status</dt>
              <dd>
                <i class="dot"></i>
                {ISSUE.status}
              </dd>
              <dt>Links</dt>
              <dd class="empty">{ISSUE.links === 0 ? 'None' : ISSUE.links}</dd>
            </dl>
            <p class="kb-absent">
              Why seven days? Should an expired link go to sign-in? The answer is in a thread somewhere, or in someone's
              head.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure>
        <figcaption class="text-sm text-fg-2">
          <strong class="font-medium text-fg">After.</strong> The decision record names it.
        </figcaption>
        <div class="panel mt-3 overflow-hidden">
          <div class="pane-bar">
            <span class="mono text-xs">ACME</span>
            <span class="sep">/</span>
            <span>Issues</span>
            <span class="sep">/</span>
            <span class="mono text-xs text-fg">{ISSUE.key}</span>
          </div>
          <div class="wf-body">
            <h3 class="wf-title mt-0">{ISSUE.title}</h3>
            <dl class="fields">
              <dt>Assignee</dt>
              <dd>
                <span class="av" aria-hidden="true">
                  {ISSUE.assignee.initials}
                </span>
                {ISSUE.assignee.name}
              </dd>
              <dt>Status</dt>
              <dd>
                <i class="dot"></i>
                {ISSUE.status}
              </dd>
              <dt>Links</dt>
              <dd class="empty">{ISSUE.links === 0 ? 'None' : ISSUE.links}</dd>
            </dl>
            <div class="ref">
              <p class="lbl">Referenced by</p>
              <p class="font-medium">{DECISION.title}</p>
              <p class="mt-1 text-xs text-fg-2">{DECISION_META.updated}</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <ul class="mt-10 md:mt-14 grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-x-8 kb-facts">
      <li>
        <h3 class="h3">Written first still counts.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          An article that mentions a key before the issue exists is listed as soon as the issue does.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3 class="h3">Resolved keys are struck through.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          Once the issue is resolved, its key in the article reads as done, so the text stays honest.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3 class="h3">Code is not a reference.</h3>
        <p class="prose mt-2 text-base">
          A key inside a code block stays plain text, so a pasted log does not link every issue it prints.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .kb-absent {
    margin-top: 16px;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    border: 1px dashed var(--border-strong);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 20px;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }
  .kb-facts {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .kb-facts li {
    padding: 22px 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .kb-facts li {
      border-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
</style>
